{"author":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nIt changes low-level, correctness-critical git reference update and locking behavior across multiple writers (checkpoint store + OPF rewrite paths) and warrants final human review despite strong regression testing.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003ePull request overview\u003c/summary\u003e\n\nThis PR fixes a race between pre-push OPF checkpoint ref rewrites and persistent checkpoint writers by making OPF ref updates participate in the same cross-process locking + native Git compare-and-swap protocol used by persistent checkpoint writes.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add `checkpoint.CASPersistentRef` to perform native `git update-ref` CAS under the existing per-reference persistent-ref flock.\n- Route both OPF rewrite paths (v1 branch rewrite and per-checkpoint ref rewrites) through `CASPersistentRef` instead of go-git’s `CheckAndSetReference`.\n- Introduce a shared native-Git CAS implementation in `gitrepo.CompareAndSwapRef` and add regression tests covering lock contention and CAS conflicts.\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eFile summaries\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_opf_rewrite.go | Switch v1 ref update to use `checkpoint.CASPersistentRef` and map native CAS conflicts to `V1RefMovedError`. |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_opf_refs.go | Switch per-checkpoint ref rewrites to `checkpoint.CASPersistentRef` to avoid lost updates. |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_opf_cas_test.go | Add regression tests reproducing the lost-update window using a real `git update-ref --stdin` transaction and asserting correct contention reporting. |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/reftable.go | Ensure plumbing git subprocesses don’t inherit `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_WORK_TREE`/`GIT_INDEX_FILE` overrides via `EnvWithoutRepoOverrides()`. |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/reftable_test.go | Extend env tests to assert repo-override env vars are filtered out of plumbing git subprocesses. |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/ref_cas.go | Add native-Git transactional CAS helper (`CompareAndSwapRef`) with error classification for CAS conflicts vs lock contention and symbolic-ref rejection. |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/ref_cas_test.go | Add cross-backend (files/reftable) tests for CAS behavior, cancellation lock release, env override immunity, and stderr classification. |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/shadow_ref.go | Clarify `ErrShadowRefBusy` semantics to cover both stale state and native lock contention. |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent_ref_update.go | Reuse new native CAS helper, add `CASPersistentRef`, and ensure persistent-ref writers/OPF writers share the same locking/CAS protocol. |\r\n| cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent_ref_update_test.go | Add tests for `CASPersistentRef` lock waiting/deadline behavior, symbolic-ref rejection, and lock-retry behavior. |\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eReview details\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 10/10 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n💡 \u003ca href=\"/entireio/cli/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAdd a `code-review` agent skill\u003c/a\u003e or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. \u003ca href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eLearn more in the docs.\u003c/a\u003e","commit_id":"fc410717c4124641346cdc83f91bb9a71a2f847f","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211#pullrequestreview-5102124583","id":5102124583,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-09-03T12:53:36Z"}
{"author":"Soph","body":"Re-reviewed at fc410717c. All three findings from my last pass are fixed, and so is the `gitPlumbingEnv` note — the flock change is fully reverted (the diff against main for `internal/flock/` is now empty), the 2s bound is gone, and the SIGKILL path now closes stdin instead. I verified the new `cmd.Cancel` behaves as intended on git 2.50.1: with an explicit `start` in the stream, stdin EOF aborts at STARTED and PREPARED, leaving the ref unchanged, exit 0, and no leftover `.lock`. Deleting that block does fail `TestPreparedRefCASCancellationReleasesGitLock`.\n\nOne correction to my earlier review: I questioned whether holding the transaction prepared across the `symbolic-ref` fork was necessary. It is, and more so than the code says. `option no-deref` + `update \u003csymref\u003e \u003cnew\u003e \u003cold\u003e` **succeeds** and converts the symref to a hash ref — git verifies the old value against the dereferenced target while writing the raw one — so without the probe the CAS compares against the wrong ref and destroys the symref. I also confirmed a prepared transaction blocks a concurrent `git symbolic-ref`. That ordering is load-bearing; worth a comment saying so, since it looks removable.\n\nFour comments inline. The first is the one I would want changed before merge — it is the same shape as my previous two: the remedy fails worse than the bug.\n\nTwo minor ones not worth inlining. `finish` (ref_cas.go) reads `commit: ok` and then calls `wait()`; a cancel in that gap makes `wait` discard a nil `cmd.Wait()` and return `ctx.Err()`, so a write that succeeded is reported as a failure. Self-healing (local v1 already points at the rewritten tip and the next push stops at the trailer watermark) but it is a lies-about-the-outcome path in code whose job is not lying about ref outcomes. And `CompareAndSwapRef`'s `errors.Join(symbolic, tx.abort())` means a lock error from the abort makes `errors.Is(err, ErrRefLocked)` true as well, so a symbolic ref could be retried 16 times — check `ErrRefSymbolic` first, or don't join.\n\nThings I checked and found correct, so they don't need defending: the injection defence (go-git's `Validate` rejects backslash and whitespace per component, so no C-style escape or extra line can reach git's quoted-arg parser — the newline test covers a family), error-classification wording against real git on both backends, transaction bookkeeping (no leaks, no double-wait, no pipe-fill deadlock, scanner limit fails into abort), the sha256-correct zero OID, and that both regression tests are genuinely red when the writers go back to `CheckAndSetReference`. `-race` clean, `mise run lint` 0 issues, no flakiness across repeated runs.","commit_id":"fc410717c4124641346cdc83f91bb9a71a2f847f","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211#pullrequestreview-5102863171","id":5102863171,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-09-03T13:59:11Z"}
