{"author":"MuskanPaliwal","body":"I went into this thinking an extra lock would make the OPF update safer, but this review showed the opposite. Git's CAS already protects the write, and the extra lock only gave this path another way to hang. That was a useful correction to my mental model.\n\nI've pushed the fixes and updated the description. One thing I'm still wondering about is whether native Git CAS should stay a small helper for direct refs, or eventually become the one path for every ref mutation we own.\n\n@soph, could you take another look when you have a chance?\n","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211#issuecomment-5527882625"}
